# SemText npl-mode — cognitive lens declaration, four render variants
# Direction A "Slate Console" (house style shared with the other tag prompts).
# npl-mode is display-only: it has TWO display states (default / primary mark)
# and no view toggles; its variants are the authoring forms the schema and the
# vocabulary CSS promise. One example page per variant, in one frame.
#
# MODE 1 — element form, default (no primary mark):
#   visible: one row of unmarked lens chips — rounded-full pills, hairline
#     slate border, slate surface fill, one near-white label per pill, one
#     pill per typed lens child, small gaps between pills, the row on its own
#     line inside a dark slate case card.
#   must never: tint or bold any pill in this panel (the default state is
#     deliberately quiet); occlude or blur a label; invent a pill for an
#     untyped lens child (an untyped child contributes no chip).
# MODE 2 — element form, primary (`primary` on the element):
#   visible: the same chip row with EVERY pill carrying the primary mark —
#     an accent-blue border, a low-opacity blue tint fill, and a slightly
#     bolder label. Labels stay fully legible on the tint.
#   must never: mark only some pills (the primary mark is whole-set); make
#     the mark an opaque or inverted block that hides the label; add focus
#     rings, buttons, toggles or any interactive chrome (display-only).
# MODE 3 — class-alias form (`.npl-mode[data-primary]`):
#   visible: a chip row visually IDENTICAL to mode 2 — same pill geometry,
#     same accent border, same tint strength, same label weight. The
#     dual-form invariant: the alternative authoring spelling renders
#     pixel-identically.
#   must never: differ from mode 2 in border, tint, weight, spacing or
#     pill count.
# MODE 4 — JS-off (vocabulary-only, light theme):
#   visible: the same declaration in the light theme with NO chips and NO
#   generated chrome — the authored lens names read as ordinary plain-prose
#   text lines inside the light case card (grey-dark text on near-white),
#   proving nothing is generated and nothing hidden without the script.
#   must never: show pills, borders, badges, tier markers or loading
#     affordances; differ in structure from the authored source order.
#
# Reference snapshots: the render-fixture captures of the privately built
# bundle + shipped vocabulary CSS in .tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-mode/
# (see reports/tag-npl-mode.md), plus the harness source view of the
# reference page. The attachments below are live paths.
schema: '0.4'
id: reference-npl-mode
type: image
quality: high
service: gemini
model: gemini-2.5-flash-image

prompt:
  text: |
    Dark-mode UI mockup of four reference-page panels in a two-by-two grid
    illustrating one cognitive-lens declaration tag in its four render
    variants, wide 16:9, flat technical illustration (screenshot-like, not
    3D). Dark slate navy background (#0F172A) with a barely visible thin
    grid and a faint blue radial glow upper-left. Each panel is a dark slate
    card (#1E293B) with a thin slate hairline border, rounded corners, deep
    soft shadow, and a small dim caption bar above it; panels are separated
    by thin slate hairlines.

    Every panel shows the same anatomy: a case card containing ONE row of
    small rounded-full chips (pills). A pill has a hairline border, a flat
    surface fill, generous horizontal padding, and ONE short bright
    near-white label bar centered inside; pills sit in a loose row with small
    gaps. All copy is abstract placeholder bars — strictly no letters,
    digits, or words.

    Top-left panel — MODE 1, default state: three pills with slate hairline
    borders and plain surface fill, no tint anywhere, labels in muted
    near-white. The quiet baseline.
    Top-right panel — MODE 2, primary state: three pills of the same size
    and spacing, but every pill has a blue (#60A5FA) border, a low-opacity
    blue tint fill (about 12% over the surface), and a slightly bolder
    brighter label. Legibility untouched — the label bar reads crisply on
    the tint.
    Bottom-left panel — MODE 3, the class-alias authoring spelling: a chip
    row INDISTINGUISHABLE from mode 2 — identical pill geometry, identical
    blue border and tint strength, identical label weight and pill count
    (the point of this panel is that the alternative spelling renders
    pixel-identically).
    Bottom-right panel — MODE 4, the JS-off light theme: the same case card
    on a near-white page (#FAFAFA panel) with NO pills at all — three short
    grey-slate plain-text lines reading as ordinary prose, proving the
    vocabulary alone generates nothing and hides nothing.
  negative: legible text, letters, numbers, digits, words, captions,
    typography, watermark, logo, 3D, photorealism, faces, avatars, robot
    mascots, more than four panels, buttons, toggles, switches, focus rings,
    progress spinners, blurred or struck-through text, an opaque or inverted
    chip fill that hides a label, half-marked chip sets (some pills tinted
    and some not in the primary panels), pills in the light JS-off panel
  style: flat dark-mode product UI illustration, rounded card corners,
    hairline borders, slate and blue palette, pill-shaped chip labels, four
    panel variant comparison

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1600
    height: 900
    aspect_ratio: '16:9'

attachments:
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-mode/fixture-enhanced-1280.png
    role: reference
    description: shipped vocabulary render, dark theme — default, primary,
      class-alias, untyped-skipped, wide-wrap and prose-context cases stacked
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-mode/fixture-enhanced-narrow-360.png
    role: reference
    description: narrow (360px) render — chip wrap behaviour inside the case cards
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-mode/fixture-jsoff-1280.png
    role: reference
    description: JS-off render — empty case boxes, no generated chrome
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-mode/npl-mode-fullpage-1280.png
    role: reference
    description: the reference page's source view of the authored example at 1280

requirements:
  subject: four panels of one cognitive-lens declaration — default chip row,
    primary-marked chip row, class-alias chip row rendered identically, and
    the JS-off light plain-prose panel
  palette: slate navy background, slate panels, hairline borders, blue
    (#60A5FA) for the primary mark border and tint, near-white pill labels
  typography: none rendered — abstract placeholder bars only
